# apt.systemd.daily conffile backup: tar warns about files removed on package upgrade
^\w{3} [ :[:digit:]]{11} [._[:alnum:]-]+ apt.systemd.daily\[[[:digit:]]+\]: tar: (Exiting with failure status due to previous errors|\.remove-on-upgrade .* Not found in archive)$
^[[:digit:]]{4}-[[:digit:]]{2}-[[:digit:]]{2}T[[:digit:]]{2}:[[:digit:]]{2}:[[:digit:]]{2}\.[[:digit:]]+[+-][[:digit:]]{2}:[[:digit:]]{2} [._[:alnum:]-]+ apt.systemd.daily\[[[:digit:]]+\]: tar: (Exiting with failure status due to previous errors|\.remove-on-upgrade .* Not found in archive)$
# package postinst re-ensuring users/groups on upgrade: rsyslog syslog/adm
# 🤖 2026-10-28: generalised, libvirt does the same for bas/libvirt
^\w{3} [ :[:digit:]]{11} [._[:alnum:]-]+ adduser\[[[:digit:]]+\]: (The system user `syslog' already exists\. Exiting\.|The user `[[:alnum:]_-]+' is already a member of `[[:alnum:]_-]+'\.)$
^[[:digit:]]{4}-[[:digit:]]{2}-[[:digit:]]{2}T[[:digit:]]{2}:[[:digit:]]{2}:[[:digit:]]{2}\.[[:digit:]]+[+-][[:digit:]]{2}:[[:digit:]]{2} [._[:alnum:]-]+ adduser\[[[:digit:]]+\]: (The system user `syslog' already exists\. Exiting\.|The user `[[:alnum:]_-]+' is already a member of `[[:alnum:]_-]+'\.)$
# 🤖 2026-10-28: unattended-upgrade-shutdown (re)started by an upgrade: Python deprecation warning, 2 lines
^\w{3} [ :[:digit:]]{11} [._[:alnum:]-]+ unattended-upgrade-shutdown\[[[:digit:]]+\]: (/usr/share/unattended-upgrades/unattended-upgrade-shutdown:[[:digit:]]+: PyGIDeprecationWarning: GLib\.unix_signal_add is deprecated; use GLibUnix\.signal_add instead|  GLib\.unix_signal_add\(GLib\.PRIORITY_DEFAULT, sig,)$
^[[:digit:]]{4}-[[:digit:]]{2}-[[:digit:]]{2}T[[:digit:]]{2}:[[:digit:]]{2}:[[:digit:]]{2}\.[[:digit:]]+[+-][[:digit:]]{2}:[[:digit:]]{2} [._[:alnum:]-]+ unattended-upgrade-shutdown\[[[:digit:]]+\]: (/usr/share/unattended-upgrades/unattended-upgrade-shutdown:[[:digit:]]+: PyGIDeprecationWarning: GLib\.unix_signal_add is deprecated; use GLibUnix\.signal_add instead|  GLib\.unix_signal_add\(GLib\.PRIORITY_DEFAULT, sig,)$
